<title>FRANCE: Axa share rises on stake buyback.</title>
<headline>Axa share rises on stake buyback.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French insurer Axa were 1.2 percent higher at midday on Friday after the group announced it had bought back Italian insurer Generali's 10.8 percent stake in Axa for 5.9 billion francs.</p>
<p>Brokers said the repurchase of the stake, which Generali started building up in 1988, removed the pressure of a stock overhang.</p>
<p>&quot;There was concern it might have gone on the market, but they've bypassed the market,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Axa's stock was up 3.40 francs at 288.40 at 1050 GMT. The bourse's CAC-40 index was down 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
